/*
    Purge of the live QA residue of 21-24 Sep 2026 (rounds QA-TEST L4, QA-LIVE-0923, QA-LIVE-0924,
    QA-UI-0924, QA-PORTAL-0924).  --  DBA script, not a migration. Development database only.

    What it removes (every row was inventoried first; the numbers are the dry-run counts of 24 Sep 2026):
      - the 4 soft-deleted test students 10112-10115 with their finance, payment, year-result and
        reconciliation rows (30 rows);
      - the QA staff accounts qa_test_user1, sa-test-c6d90a47, qa2_105935, qa2_034943, qa_ui_040147,
        qa_ui2_042658, the 4 QA-* roles, the 4 QA-* groups, the QA-UI pages/API link/permissions/report (34);
      - the 84 approval requests the rounds created (20867-20869, 21644-21724) with their 203 steps and
        345 history rows, approval configuration 21 and its level 38;
      - 79 soft-deleted code-list rows (codes QA_*, QA1*, QAT_*, QAUI*) in 17 MOHECORE.LU_* tables;
      - portal inquiries 3 and 4, information requests 949-951, the two QA uploads of student 2 (3624,
        3625) and their history rows; budget appropriation 1 and chart-of-accounts rows 2967/2968.
    What it puts back:
      - the finance rows of students 3 and 1003, which the tests set to Received with a QA note / cheque id,
        to the values recorded in approval requests 20867 and 21667 (status NOT_SPECIFIED, as V135 maps it);
      - the same status/cheque date on seeded students 10065/10066, whose finance rows the scope seed copied
        from student 3 after that edit; the QA-TEST note on archive snapshot 945 of student 4.
    Left alone on purpose: AUDITLOG.AuditLogs / AuditTrail and UMSCORE.UserActions (audit trail of the
    rounds -- 256 + 28 rows mention QA), the 40 ZZ-SCOPE-SEED students (dev data, DEC-23), the sample-data
    seeds and ZZ_NOTIFICATION_SETTINGS_BEFORE_SEED (own restore scripts), approval requests 21148/21149
    (untagged edits of student 1 on 22 Sep), finance-archive entry 1 and archive row 1 (deleted by the
    probes; restore from backup as the reports say).

    Every DELETE names its ids and a text guard, so it is a no-op on a database where the rows are gone.
    Dry-run by default: set @Commit = 1 to keep the changes. Sets TenantAll and TenantWafarWrite itself
    (WAFAR_RECONCILIATION has a BEFORE DELETE block predicate keyed on the second one).

        sqlcmd -S localhost,1433 -d MOHE -I -f 65001 -b -i purge_qa_live_test_residue.sql
*/
SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT ON;

DECLARE @Commit BIT = 0;   /* 1 = keep the changes; 0 = run everything, print the counts, roll back */

EXEC sp_set_session_context @key = N'TenantAll',        @value = N'1';
EXEC sp_set_session_context @key = N'TenantWafarWrite', @value = N'1';

DECLARE @n INT, @total INT = 0;
BEGIN TRAN;

/* ---- Code-list rows created by the code-list tests (delete = soft delete in the app) ---- */
DELETE FROM MOHECORE.[LU_APPROVAL_REQUEST_TYPE] WHERE (CODE LIKE 'QA[-_0-9]%' OR CODE LIKE 'QAT[_]%' OR CODE LIKE 'QAUI%') AND IS_SYSTEM = 0 AND (NAME_EN LIKE '%QA%' OR NAME_AR LIKE '%QA%');
